  "id": "COMPOUND:31997 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Chakasaponin Ii is implicated in the regulation of Neuropilin-2 through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Chakasaponin Ii acts as a target for several enzymes, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn targets Neuropilin-2. This indicates a direct enzymatic interaction between Chakasaponin Ii and Neuropilin-2, potentially through the modulation of sialylation processes. Additionally, Chakasaponin Ii is also shown to target Chaxamycin B, which further targets Neuropilin-2, reinforcing the notion of a multi-tiered regulatory mechanism involving Neuropilin-2. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Chakasaponin Ii in modulating Neuropilin-2 activity, possibly through the inhibition of sialyltransferase enzymes. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Chakasaponin Ii and Neuropilin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
